{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFZSQ5MmnysmYBSxXrgu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] When the fake `hermes plugins validate` fails, `doctor` exits non-zero\n\n`hermes-tiiny-router doctor` is done. All six checklist items pass, and the full `npm test` run passes (40 tests plus the Python suite). Everything is committed except `.redeye/notes.md`, as instructed.\n\n**What it does:** it prints one `PASS`, `WARN` or `FAIL` line per check, then exits 1 if any check failed. The checks are:\n1. The installed directory exists, has our manifest, and no file is missing.\n2. The installed version matches `package.json`.\n3. No installed file differs from the manifest.\n4. `hermes plugins validate` accepts the directory.\n5. `hermes config get delegation.backend` returns `tiiny-router`.\n6. `python3` is on the PATH.\n7. The device answers. An unreachable device or a missing key is only a warning.\n\nThe device check runs a short Python script that imports the installed `scripts/tiiny_ctl.py` and requests `/models` from the device. If a check throws, for example because `hermes` isn't on the PATH, that check is marked `FAIL` and the rest still run. The code is in `src/doctor.ts`, with a small output-capturing helper added to `src/hermes.ts`.\n\n**Test harness change:** your shell has a real `TIINY_API_KEY`, and the device answered during the first run. So `test/harness.ts` now removes all `TIINY_*` variables and points every run at a fake key and a closed local port. No test can reach the real device now. The fake `hermes` also answers `config get KEY` from a new `hermesConfig` option.\n\n**Open points:**\n- **Unconfirmed output format:** I assumed the real `hermes config get KEY` prints only the value, because `SKILL.md` uses it that way. If it prints `key: value` instead, the backend check will report a failure on a correct setup. It's worth running once against a real Hermes.\n- **Stale copies:** `doctor` doesn't look for a stale copy in the Hermes source tree. The ticket made that optional.\n- **No README:** this branch has no `README.md` yet, so `doctor` is only described in the command's usage text and in `AGENTS.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":552,"cache_read_input_tokens":85281,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":552},"output_tokens":716,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eaf71b4b-c4bc-4224-8c85-0667019f1ee8","uuid":"0f73663e-274b-4fd0-b42e-690f9799accb","timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:58:09.223Z","request_id":"req_011ChFZSPthQ1n9zFCrHRQEn"}
